5. Collection vs Stream
==============================================================================

Collection
----------
Stores and manages data.

Code:

List<String> names =
    new ArrayList<>();

names.add("Java");
names.add("Spring");

Output:
[Java, Spring]


Stream
------
Processes data from a source.

Code:

List<String> result =
    names.stream()
         .map(String::toUpperCase)
         .toList();

Output:
[JAVA, SPRING]

Difference:
Collection = Data storage
Stream     = Data processing pipeline

Collection = Reusable
Stream     = Single-use

Collection = Supports add/remove
Stream     = Does not modify its source directly

Interview One-Liner:
A Collection stores data, while a Stream performs declarative
processing over data.

