6. peek() vs map()
==============================================================================

peek()
------
Observes elements without transforming them.

Input:
["java", "spring"]

Code:

List<String> result =
    List.of("java", "spring")
        .stream()
        .peek(System.out::println)
        .toList();

Console Output:
java
spring

Result:
[java, spring]


map()
-----
Transforms elements into new values.

Input:
["java", "spring"]

Code:

List<String> result =
    List.of("java", "spring")
        .stream()
        .map(String::toUpperCase)
        .toList();

Output:
[JAVA, SPRING]

Difference:
peek() = Observe or debug
map()  = Transform

Interview One-Liner:
Use map() for transformation and use peek() sparingly for debugging,
not for critical business side effects.

