7. forEach() vs forEachOrdered()
==============================================================================

forEach()
---------
Processes every element, but parallel execution may not preserve order.

Input:
[1, 2, 3, 4]

Code:

List.of(1,2,3,4)
    .parallelStream()
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Possible Output:
3
4
2
1


forEachOrdered()
----------------
Processes elements in encounter order.

Code:

List.of(1,2,3,4)
    .parallelStream()
    .forEachOrdered(System.out::println);

Output:
1
2
3
4

Difference:
forEach()        = Order not guaranteed in parallel execution
forEachOrdered() = Encounter order maintained

Interview One-Liner:
Use forEachOrdered() when order is mandatory, but remember that
preserving order can reduce parallel performance.

