8. groupingBy() vs partitioningBy()
==============================================================================

groupingBy()
------------
Creates any number of groups based on a classifier.

Input:
["one", "two", "java", "spring"]

Code:

Map<Integer, List<String>> result =
    List.of("one","two","java","spring")
        .stream()
        .collect(
            Collectors.groupingBy(
                String::length));

Output:
{
 3=[one, two],
 4=[java],
 6=[spring]
}


partitioningBy()
----------------
Creates exactly two Boolean groups.

Input:
[1, 2, 3, 4]

Code:

Map<Boolean, List<Integer>> result =
    List.of(1,2,3,4)
        .stream()
        .collect(
            Collectors.partitioningBy(
                n -> n % 2 == 0));

Output:
{
 false=[1, 3],
 true=[2, 4]
}

Difference:
groupingBy()     = Multiple keys or groups
partitioningBy() = true and false groups

Interview One-Liner:
Use groupingBy() for multi-category classification and
partitioningBy() for Boolean conditions.

